~ initialize_local_variables
do Variables.add_local("childhood", false)
do Variables.add_local("family", false)
do Variables.add_local("day", false)
do Variables.add_local("yday", false)
do Variables.add_local("dreams", 0)
do Variables.add_local("fingers", false)
do Variables.add_local("toes", false)
do Variables.add_local("breathe", false)
do Variables.add_local("eyes", false)
do Variables.add_local("questions", 0)
=> start

~ start
You went to bed early tonight, feeling especially tired after a long day at work.
Staring at the ceiling, hours passed you by. It's way past midnight, now. You're almost asleep, half-thinking, half-dreaming. 
What about? => about

~ about
...
- My childhood. [if Variables.get_var("childhood") == false]
	Memories forgotten, unwillingly unearthed.[do Variables.set_var("childhood", true)][do Variables.mod_var("dreams", 1)]
	Buildings, larger than life. Planes, cars, buses, loud. Food you wouldn't eat. Leftovers?
	A friend? Just not a very good one. Wouldn't ever let you play with their toys.
	Were you poor? No. Not really. But it sure felt that way. 
	Another friend. A dog. Gone too soon. 
	Your parents loved you. They did all they could, but you resented them for it.
	Eh, you can't blame yourself. You were young. Kids are pricks. 
	What else? => about
- My family. [if Variables.get_var("family") == false]
	Mom. Dad. Two older brothers. A sister. Younger?[do Variables.set_var("family", true)][do Variables.mod_var("dreams", 1)]
	Voices. Whispers. Screams. A handful of blurred faces and hushed voices. Can you really not remember them? 
	They call to you. It gets louder and quieter in equal measure. 
	Shame on you, they say. Then they leave. 
	You've had this dream before, a few times. But these people mean nothing to you, now. 
	What else? => about
- The day it all began. [if Variables.get_var("day") == false]
	The day all what began?[do Variables.set_var("day", true)][do Variables.mod_var("dreams", 1)]
	Oh. Right. 
	You vaguely remember crows filling up the sky. Could barely see anything anymore. Your parents thought it was an eclipse. 
	Then they were gone. The sky turned red, a lot of people died, you survived. End of story. 
	You were too young to understand what was happening. Or to remember much else. 
	The Cullings, as people have fittingly named them, have been occuring periodically ever since. 
	You were placed in foster care, then left the day you turned eighteen. That's it. 
	What else? => about
- Yesterday. [if Variables.get_var("yday") == false]
	The usual. Helped around any way you could. Got paid for it. Came home.[do Variables.set_var("yday", true)][do Variables.mod_var("dreams", 1)]
	Watched some TV. A new tape your coworker gave you. Some old show from way back when, about a serial killer heartthrob. Complete non-sense. 
	It was nice of her, either way. 
	...Or was that the day before?
	You try your heardest to remember. You can't. 
	Today will be the same. 
	What else? => about
- Just... stop. [if Variables.get_var("dreams") >= 2]


~ dream
It all feels rather... generic. Impersonal. These thoughts, or dreams, leave you cold and empty. No twitching muscles, no elevated heart-rate, no sweat.
Are these bland memories really yours? 
[speed=0.6]It's all brought to a stop by... something. A gust of wind you can barely feel. 
[speed=0.6]It's cold, all of a sudden. Colder than you've ever felt.
[speed=0.6]Are you awake now?
- Yes.
	[speed=0.6]How can you be sure? => react
- No. 
	[speed=0.6]That's right. You aren't. Wake up. => react 
- I... don't know?
	[speed=0.6]Time to find out. => react

~ react
[speed=0.6]...
- Flex your fingers. [if Variables.get_var("fingers") == false]
	[speed=0.6]You can't. [do Variables.set_var("fingers", true)][do Variables.mod_var("questions", 1)] => react
- Move your toes. [if Variables.get_var("toes") == false]
	[speed=0.6]Nothing happens. [do Variables.set_var("toes", true)][do Variables.mod_var("questions", 1)] => react
- Breathe. [if Variables.get_var("questions") >= 3]
	[speed=0.6]You're not breathing anymore. 
	- Panic. 
		[speed=0.6]You can't. => hours
	- Relax. 
		[speed=0.6]You can't.
		- Panic. 
			[speed=0.6]Can't do that either. => hours
- Open your eyes. [if Variables.get_var("questions") >= 2 && Variables.get_var("eyes") == false]
	[speed=0.6]The eyelids give way. Your eyes are open now. [do Variables.set_var("eyes", true)][do Variables.mod_var("questions", 1)]
	[speed=0.6]It doesn't change a thing, however. Everything around you is shrouded in darkness, your vision as useless as it was when they were closed. 
	- Look around. 
		[speed=0.6]Your eyes move freely. Your head, however, is firmly stuck in place. Everything is darkness. 
		- Cry for help. 
			[speed=0.6]Your mouth can't open. Your vocal cords are a thing of the past. 
			[speed=0.6]Nobody could hear you, anyway. => react
		- Keep your mouth shut. 
			[speed=0.6]Finally, something you can do. => react
	- Cry for help. 
		[speed=0.6]Your mouth can't open. Your vocal cords are a thing of the past. 
		[speed=0.6]Nobody could hear you, anyway. => react
	
~ hours
[speed=0.2]...Minutes which might as well be hours pass. The cold is as numbing as the paralyzing fear. 
[speed=0.6]All of a sudden, you hear a sound. [do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_crow_goddess")]A caw. And then another. 
The cold subsides. It is replaced by warmth and peacefulness.
Your paralysis demon took their sweet time to show up. A... crow? 
A one-eyed crow. It lands on your thigh. => hello

~ hello
Crow: It's so good to finally meet you, Keeper.
- Am I... dead?
	Crow: Not quite, my child. 
	Crow: Death shall have no dominion over you any longer. 
	Crow: You shall know happiness and power the likes of which feeble human minds can scarcely fathom. 
	Crow: You are, indeed, reborn. You are cleansed, and you are freed.
	Crow: But do not grieve your former self, for you are mine now, mind and flesh.
	- I...
		You try to speak, but no words come out. 
		Your thoughts trickle out of your head, one by one. Your mind is gone. => fear
