~ fear
Crow: I sense your fear, dearest Keeper. Give in to the light, to the warmth that is now washing over you. 
Crow: I've been watching you. I know you. I know your soul. Your mind and body may be forged anew, but your soul is something I've no sway over. 
Crow: But I must trust it with my life, for I have no other choice. 
Crow: I'm here to set you on your path. To guide, as I've done twice before, as I will four times more.  
Crow: I bestow upon you my Gift of Sight. You shall see things where others cannot. Use it wisely, and with love.
Crow: Go to a village up in the mountains. The village all these lowly heretics speak falsehoods about. 
Crow: Go to (village name, game name?). My home. My church.
Crow: A place untouched by the Cullings, where a third one shall grow, a third one shall die, a third one shall live, and a third one shall fly. 
#potential pop up: hmmm, that doesnt quite add up...
